# DROP AUDIO PACKS IN HERE. This is the only folder in the repository that
# keeps sound files at all.
#
# It exists because of a near miss. The Quaternius bundle contains an Audio
# folder, 27 MB on disk — and measured against the rules for
# models3d/_incoming/packs it came to ZERO, because that folder keeps model and
# image formats and nothing else. Moved there, every sound would have been
# discarded without a word, which is precisely how eight character packs
# vanished on 22 Aug and were not noticed for nine days.
#
# The runtime synthesises its effects (see the sound engine in
# joshrix3d-1.js), so nothing here is load-bearing yet — but a real recorded
# sample is a thing the platform has never had, and losing one to a filter
# would be losing it for nothing.
#
# Run `node tools/check-incoming.mjs audio` after any upload; it prints what
# survives, per pack, and names anything that would land empty.

# ignore everything...
*

# ...but descend into directories
!*/

# ...and keep the formats a browser can actually play
!*.wav
!*.ogg
!*.mp3
!*.m4a
!*.flac
!*.aac
!*.opus
!*.webm

# licence files travel with the assets they cover
!LICENSE*
!License*
!license*
!*.txt

!README.md
!.gitignore
